@startuml process-flow
title XML to JSON Publisher – Process Flow

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor<<fail>> #F8CECC
  BorderColor<<fail>> #B85450
  BackgroundColor<<ok>> #D5E8D4
  BorderColor<<ok>> #82B366
}

|Client|
start
:POST /upload-xml
(multipart/form-data,
one or more "file" parts);

|Controller|
:XmlToJsonPublisherController.uploadXml;
:For each uploaded MultipartFile,
call XmlProcessorService.processXmlContent(fileName, bytes);
note right
  Each call is @Async – dispatched to the
  ThreadPoolTaskExecutor (AsyncConfiguration).
  Pool size & queue capacity = ASYNC_POOL_SIZE.
  RejectedExecutionHandler = CallerRunsPolicy,
  so once pool+queue are full the calling
  (request) thread runs the task itself
  instead of the request failing.
end note

fork
|#LightBlue|Async Worker (per file)|
:Extract content_id via StAX pull-parser
(XmlUtil.getXmlAttributeValueFromStream);
note right
  Fresh XMLInputFactory per call – not a
  shared bean (thread-unsafe symbol table
  cache). DTD & external entities disabled
  (XXE / billion-laughs mitigation).
end note

if (content_id present\nand non-blank?) then (no)
  :FileOutcome(fileName, false,\n"Content ID is empty.");<<fail>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Acquire ReentrantLock for this content_id
(ContentLockRegistry);
note right
  Per-content_id lock, not a global lock –
  concurrent uploads of *different*
  content_ids still run fully in parallel.
end note

if (Saver.exists(content_id)?\n(re-checked now that\nthe lock is held)) then (yes)
  :Release lock;
  :FileOutcome(fileName, false,\nAlreadyProcessedException message);<<fail>>
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Validate against XSD
(XmlValidator + Schema bean,\nJavaxXmlConfiguration);
note right
  Schema is the thread-safe singleton bean;
  a fresh Validator (schema.newValidator())
  is created per call.
end note

if (schema valid?) then (no)
  :Release lock;
  :FileOutcome(fileName, false,\nSAXException message);<<fail>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Transform XML → JSON
(XmlTransformer: Saxon-HE Xslt30Transformer
running judgment-to-json.xsl,
XSLT 3.0 xsl:map / array{} → JSON);
:Deserialize JSON → NormalizedJudgment
(Jackson ObjectMapper);
note right
  XsltExecutable is the thread-safe singleton
  bean (compiled once at startup); a fresh
  Xslt30Transformer (xsltExecutable.load30())
  is created per call – reusing one across
  threads would silently corrupt output.
end note

:Derive RAG-ready text
(RagTransformer: StrategyOneRagTransformer –
title as header line, paragraphs joined
by blank lines);

:Save outputs to disk
($DISK_SAVER_PATH/<content_id>/<content_id>.json
$DISK_SAVER_PATH/<content_id>/<content_id>.txt)
(Saver: DiskSaver);

:Release lock;
:FileOutcome(fileName, true, null);<<ok>>
stop

end fork

|Controller|
:Join all per-file CompletableFutures;
:Return 200 OK with
List<FileOutcome> body;

|Client|
:Receive per-file success/failure report;
stop

@enduml
